	(descr "A bought BeagleBoard.org PocketBeagle 2 (rev A1) plugged straight onto its host (boards/contracts/compute-link.md v3, 2026-11-28): two 2 x 18 2.54 mm sockets (Hong Cheng HC-PM254-8.5H-2x18PZ, 8.5 mm body) under its P1 and P2 header pins, pads 1xx = P1.xx and 2xx = P2.xx, the board seen from above its component side (SRM Fig. 3.45: rows 3.53 / 6.07 mm in from each long edge, 18 columns centred). F.Fab and User.1: the board's 55 x 35 mm outline (13.6 mm max height, SRM Table 3.2), its underside about 11.04 mm above the host [I: the header insulator]; host parts up to 8.04 mm under it. The courtyard is the two sockets only. No holes: the board has none. STAGED for the owner to install.")
